WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.000
When you program with AI, you can send several agents to explore different options at once.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The hard part becomes tracing their work, and judging it.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
There are many parameters to tweak, and agents' work is slow, costs money, and comes out different every time.

4
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:31.000
So nock breaks an experiment into stages, each branching on parameters: models, skills, anything.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Each stage's results are scored against criteria, or decide what runs next.

6
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Every stage is cached once it runs: a memoized graph that's easy to read, and saves time and money.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
You can drill into any run to see exactly what happened…

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
…or let your agent query the trends, without inventing a methodology.

9
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Trace and judge your agents' work, and choose the best way forward.
